comment0.target=SlotMachineCC2Test
comment0.text=\r\n The test class SlotMachineCC2Test.\r\n\r\n @author David Garzon, Wilson Mendivelso\r\n @version 1\r\n
comment1.target=void setUp()
comment1.text=\r\n Sets up the test fixture.\r\n\r\n Called before every test case method.\r\n
comment10.target=void accordingIcPgshouldSpinAWheel()
comment10.text=\r\n Verifies that a wheel can be spun successfully once it has been\r\n locked and then unlocked, leaving the machine status as ok.\r\n
comment11.target=void accordingCgCpShouldNotChangeConfigurationWhenWheelIsLocked()
comment11.text=\r\n Verifies that after locking a wheel with lock(), calling\r\n spin(wheel, steps) does not alter what that wheel shows in\r\n configuration().\r\n
comment12.target=void accordingCgCpShouldChangeConfigurationWhenWheelIsUnlockedAfterLock()
comment12.text=\r\n Verifies that after locking and then unlocking a wheel\r\n (lock() followed by unlock()), spin(wheel, steps) can\r\n change what that wheel shows.\r\n
comment13.target=void accordingCgHnAddSymbolShouldFailWhenColorAlreadyExists()
comment13.text=Adding a color that already exists on a wheel should fail
comment14.target=void accordingGmLaShouldNotAllowSpinningALockedWheel()
comment14.text=\r\n A locked wheel should not be able to spin.\r\n
comment15.target=void accordingMsRhShouldSwapSymbolsBetweenTwoValidWheels()
comment15.text=\r\n Verifies that swapping two valid wheels with different symbols\r\n using swap(int, int) leaves each one showing the symbol the\r\n other previously had.\r\n
comment16.target=void accordingMsRhShouldNotChangeLockedWheelWhenSpinning()
comment16.text=\r\n Verifies that a wheel locked with lock(int) does not change its\r\n visible symbol when attempting to spin it with spin(int).\r\n
comment17.target=void accordingMsRhShouldDetectJackpotAfterForcedSpin()
comment17.text=\r\n Collectively verifies that forcing a configuration where all\r\n wheels end up with the same symbol via spin(String[]) changes\r\n the system's state and successfully detects the jackpot.\r\n
comment18.target=void accordingMsRhShouldDeleteLastWheelWhenPositionGreaterThanSize()
comment18.text=\r\n Verifies that delWheel(int pos) removes the last wheel when the\r\n given position is greater than the number of wheels.\r\n
comment19.target=void accordingDrRmShouldBeJackpotWhenAllWheelsMatch()
comment19.text=\r\n A jackpot should occur when all wheels show the same color.\r\n
comment2.target=void accordingGrMsShouldNotSetSymbolsThatDoesNotExists()
comment2.text=\r\n If a symbol doesn't exists, wheels should change their symbols except \r\n that one with the strange symbol.\r\n
comment20.target=void accordingDrRmShouldKeepCorrectWheelCountAfterAddAndDelete()
comment20.text=\r\n The number of wheels should remain correct after an add and a\r\n delete.\r\n
comment21.target=void accordingFsGcShouldKeepDistinctSymbolCountAfterSwap()
comment21.text=\r\n WHAT IT SHOULD DO\: swapping two wheels should not alter the\r\n number of distinct symbols reported for the machine (swap\r\n moves the content, it does not modify it).\r\n
comment22.target=void accordingClPcShouldNotReportJackpotWhenSetConfigurationDiffers()
comment22.text=\r\n EXAMPLE 2 \u2014 "what it should NOT do"\: leaving a given\r\n configuration (spin with array) should not report a jackpot if\r\n the assigned symbols do not match each other.\r\n
comment23.target=void accordingJcSrShouldExchangeWheels()
comment23.text=\r\n Tests that two wheels can be swapped.\r\n
comment24.target=void accordingFmSnShouldShowCorrectConfiguration()
comment24.text=\r\n Tests that configuration() reports each wheel's current color\r\n
comment25.target=void accordingGmLaShouldReflectExactConfigurationAfterSpinWithGivenSymbols()
comment25.text=\r\n spin(setSymbols) should leave the machine in exactly those\r\n colors.\r\n
comment26.target=void accordingCxLxShouldAdvanceToNextSymbol()
comment26.text=\r\n Verifies that spinning a wheel advances it to the next symbol\r\n in the machine's symbol list.\r\n
comment27.target=void accordingMrSeShouldKeepLockedWheelFixedAndAllowSpinAfterUnlock()
comment27.text=\r\n Should\: a locked wheel should not move when a spin is\r\n attempted, and should be able to spin again after an unlock.\r\n
comment28.target=void accordingMrSeShouldRejectSpinSetSymbolsWhenColorMissing()
comment28.text=\r\n Should NOT\: apply any change if one of the requested colors\r\n does not exist on its corresponding wheel.\r\n
comment29.target=void accordingRlBbShouldNotSpinWhenLocked()
comment29.text=\r\n Verifies that a locked wheel cannot spin.\r\n
comment3.target=void accordingGrMsShouldNotAddStrangeSymbolsAndWinWithThatSymbol()
comment3.text=\r\n If a symbol doesn't exists it shouldn't be added and \r\n you shouldn't win if you try to set the machine with that symbol.\r\n
comment30.target=void tearDown()
comment30.text=\r\n Tears down the test fixture.\r\n\r\n Called after every test case method.\r\n
comment4.target=void accordingIcPgShouldNotSwap()
comment4.text=\r\n Verifies that attempting to swap two wheels fails when one of\r\n them is locked, setting the machine status to not ok.\r\n
comment5.target=void shouldNotSwap()
comment5.text=\r\n Verifies that attempting to swap two wheels fails when one of\r\n them is locked, setting the machine status to not ok.\r\n
comment6.target=void accordingCcGbShouldNotSpinLockedWheel()
comment6.text=\r\n A locked wheel does not advance when the machine spins.\r\n
comment7.target=void accordingCcGbShouldSpinAfterUnlock()
comment7.text=\r\n A wheel that was locked resumes spinning after unlock.\r\n
comment8.target=void accordingBaGqShouldLockWheel()
comment8.text=\ Prueba que una rueda existente pueda ser bloqueada correctamente.\r\n La maquina debe permitir bloquear una rueda que existe.\r\n La operacion debe realizarse correctamente y ok() debe retornar true.\r\n
comment9.target=void accordingBaGqShouldNotSpinLockedWheel()
comment9.text=\ Prueba que una rueda bloqueada no pueda girar.\r\n \u00BFQue no deberia hacer? * Una rueda que se encuentra bloqueada no debe avanzar\r\ncuando se intenta realizar un spinStep.
